<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2358] Write behind store swallows exception trace in case of error</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2358</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;See &lt;tt&gt;GridCacheWriteBehindStore:708&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;LT.warn(log, e, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;Unable to update underlying store: &quot;&lt;/span&gt; + store);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The exception trace is never printed out in case of warnings, therefore user sees only message, which is usually not enough.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12929377">IGNITE-2358</key>
            <summary>Write behind store swallows exception trace in case of error</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
